From: alvesmaicon <alvesmaiconn@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: simple-amplifier: power up after the output driver feeding it

The amplifier's DRV widget and the output driver feeding it are often
both out_drv widgets, so DAPM sorts them by register: DRV has none
(SND_SOC_NOPM) and comes first. On the A33 that driver is the codec's
Headphone Amp, which sleeps 700 ms when it powers up so its output can
settle. With the speaker amplifier already on, the speaker plays that
whole ramp as hiss and a pop before every sound.

Give DRV a subsequence of 1: it now powers up after the other out_drv
widgets and down before them.

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/simple-amplifier.c b/sound/soc/codecs/simple-amplifier.c
index ca53b08..6342e02 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/simple-amplifier.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/simple-amplifier.c
@@ -117,8 +117,18 @@ static int simple_amp_power_event(struct snd_soc_dapm_widget *w,
 static const struct snd_soc_dapm_widget simple_amp_dapm_widgets[] = {
 	SND_SOC_DAPM_INPUT("INL"),
 	SND_SOC_DAPM_INPUT("INR"),
-	SND_SOC_DAPM_OUT_DRV_E("DRV", SND_SOC_NOPM, 0, 0, NULL, 0, simple_amp_power_event,
-			       (SND_SOC_DAPM_POST_PMU | SND_SOC_DAPM_PRE_PMD)),
+	/*
+	 * The output driver feeding the amplifier is often an out_drv too:
+	 * sequence after it on power up and before it on power down, so the
+	 * speaker doesn't play that driver ramping up or down.
+	 */
+	{
+		.id = snd_soc_dapm_out_drv, .name = "DRV",
+		SND_SOC_DAPM_INIT_REG_VAL(SND_SOC_NOPM, 0, 0),
+		.event = simple_amp_power_event,
+		.event_flags = SND_SOC_DAPM_POST_PMU | SND_SOC_DAPM_PRE_PMD,
+		.subseq = 1,
+	},
 	SND_SOC_DAPM_OUTPUT("OUTL"),
 	SND_SOC_DAPM_OUTPUT("OUTR"),
 	SND_SOC_DAPM_REGULATOR_SUPPLY("VCC", 20, 0),
